  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA quiet morning across the area courtesy of surface high \npressure centered across the northern Great Lakes. This has \nresulted in mostly clear skies and calm flow, allowing for \nchilly temperatures and river valley fog once again southeast of\nthe Ohio River. Areas of dense fog will be possible in the \n'typical' locations, but overall, coverage is expected to be \nslightly less than that of yesterday morning. Temperatures this \nmorning will bottom out in the 40s across the lowlands, with 30s\npossible across the mountain valleys. Some patchy frost could \noccur across the typical northern mountain valley cold spots, \nsave the river valleys. \n\nSurface high pressure to the northwest will remain in control of\nthe weather through the weekend, bringing mostly clear skies \namid seasonably cool temperatures. Highs will generally be ~ 5 \ndegrees below normal, with mid 60s to low 70s across the \nlowlands, all amid light northerly breezes during the \nafternoons. Lows tomorrow morning will be a few degrees warmer \nthan this morning, with river valley fog expected east/south. A\nretrograding nor'easter could result in isolated light showers \nacross the far northeast CWA late Sunday or Sunday night, but \nany rainfall would remain light, generally 0.10\" or less. \nOtherwise, dry weather prevails.\n\nA gradual pattern shift begins early next week as a modest upper\nridge begins to shift east over the area. This results in\ncontinued dry weather into Wednesday, if not longer. Low-end \nrain chances return late Wednesday onward as a front begins to\napproach the region. Timing/placement discrepancies remain\nbetween models resulting in continued low confidence. The\noverall theme remains fairly consistent though, with mainly dry\nweather continuing through the work week, with a trend towards\nmore unsettled heading into next weekend as the front works into\nthe area amid an increasingly moist Gulf airmass. Below normal \ntemperatures on Monday will transition to near normal on \nTuesday, with slightly above expected Wednesday onward courtesy\nof persistent return flow.",
